// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P985169977" "Vanguard Wizard"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2674514142" "Urgh... what is this...?!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3580454125" "You've discovered the true identity of the Sentinel, and a way to weaken Mot."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P314327817" "The wizards relayed everything that happened, {HeroName}. I never would have thought that Marcus Valerius was the Sentinel...  truly, Mot is an evil being, a representation not only of death, but of blind, unreasonable hate. Hate, {HeroName}, that makes us forget what why we love our friends, our family. It twists the truth of the past to be the lies of the present... and those lies become what drives us. <br><br>I suppose this is a lesson for us all, {HeroName}. We can't survive on the past by just memory alone... we need something in the present to remind us about why we fight, why we live. Marcus lost that... and lost himself in the process.<br><br>Sorry, {HeroName}, this isn't a time for reflection, not just yet. We have one half of the equation, the other rests in the journals of David Hazen. Unfortunately... I have not heard from Scirocco. I fear the worst."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Bellerose 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2110083740" "{HeroName}... I remember you... you saved my life before.<br><br>It's all flooding back to me now... My life before coming to this city. I've spent too long here... Mot's minions twisted my mind... My will...<br><br>I came here looking for a challenge... something to prove my new abilities against. What I found was...<br><br>I must go, {HeroName}. I must leave this city and never return to it. Thank you for your help... I do not wish to think about what would've happen if you had not already saved me before."
// Answer Text :
"P3249836814" "Goodbye, Bellerose."
// Answer Text :
"P3215973113" "Hold on, I didn't save you for nothing. I deserve something in return."
// Page DeserveSomething Text :
"P2606817172" "I have nothing to give, {HeroName}, except my gratitude.<br><br>Now, let me leave, unless you did all of this for a selfish reason of me 'owing' you.<br><br>If that's the case... I will not hesitate to attack you where you stand with all of my might."
// Answer Text :
"P3852266835" "Alright, Bellerose, just go."
// Answer Text :
"P3365891204" "Strike -me- down? Just try it, Bellerose."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Hopp 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page SaveHopp Text :
"P3727672978" "<color orange>You see Detective Hopp laying on the ground, badly beaten by the Banished Pantheon. However, he seems to still be holding on to his life by a bare thread.</color><br><br>{HeroName}... it feels like forever ago that... you last saved me...<br><br>Mot... the Pantheon... they brought me here to suffer... to make me think life was nothing but suffering. They tried... to beat it into me... that there was no hope. But then I remembered... the time you saved me... that even in this desperate hour... even when Mot's power seems to be infinite... there's still someone who can make a stand against it... there's... there's still <i>hope</i>...<br><br>I've been hanging on to my life... hoping that something would happen... that someone would come to... to save me. Please... {HeroName}... there's an emergency... PPD teleporter... got it from... a guy named... Roy Cooling... back before I came here. I... hah...<br><br>I had finally... gotten it fixed... when the Pantheon ambushed me. Please... activate it... help me get out of here."
// Answer Text :
"P2719818141" "(Activate Hopp's PPD teleporter)"
// Answer Text :
"P1354900092" "If I save you, the PPD needs to clear my name."
// Page VillainChoice Text :
"P830805600" "I... can't do that... {HeroName}... I won't go against... The law that I've promised to uphold...<br><br>If you want... True forgiveness... You need to... earn it... on your own..."
// Answer Text :
"P2554791283" "Fine. (Activate Hopp's teleporer)"
// Answer Text :
"P3018227116" "Then you can rot here. (Leave)"
// Answer Text :
"P2282999100" "I'll just finish you off, then. (Kill Hopp)"
// Page DontSave Text :
"P3257908859" "<color orange>You see the dead body of a man who was beaten to death by the Banished Pantheon. You search through his pockets and discover that his name was Anthony Hopps, a detective for the PPD.<br><br>It seems the Banished Pantheon ensured he died in the most painful way possible, judging by the twisted expression on his face.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1798695407" "I've tried to get in touch with Scirocco, but he is not responding. I fear that Mot is aware that we're getting closer to finding his weakness and has either killed Scirocco or is in the process of doing so; it will then command its minions to destroy the last traces of Hazen's journal.<br><br>Even if we free every single person within Mot, the monster will just absorb them once again. Hazen <i>must</i> have had a way around that with the magic he used. It's a long shot yet again, {HeroName}, but our long shot from before paid off with the Sentinel."
// AcceptString :
"P2547717595" "I'll go to the office and save Scirocco."
// SendOffString :
"P2999666381" "Thank you, {HeroName}. I must continue work on my end to prepare for what might be the final battle for our world.<br><br>If Scirocco has fallen, then you must be the one who tracks down the final pieces of Hazen's journal. If what Heather Townshend said is true, it will contain the missing piece to the true purpose of Hazen's runes.<br><br>If not... well, then we'll have to hope for another miracle."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1086545055" "Find David Hazen's Missing Journal"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1326061515" "No time to talk, {HeroName}."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1079236389" "<color deepskyblue>Part 6: The Life of David Hazen</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2024840259" "You enter the old office building where the last pieces of Hazen's journal are."
